Line: "- Day 154 made this landable with the panic-path fix. The input-validation piece"

```python
lower = "- day 154 made this landable with the panic-path fix. the input-validation piece"
re.match(r"day\s+\d+", lower)  # Does this match?
```

The regex `day\s+\d+` with `re.match` only matches at the beginning of the string! The line starts with `"- "`, not `"day"`. So `re.match` fails because it's anchored to the start.

The fix: use `re.search` instead of `re.match` for the Day NNN pattern, since assessment lines often have list item prefixes like "- " or "* ".

